{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Environmental News"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Being Heard"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 17}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Conditional Sentences with <span class=\"italic\">If</span> Clause"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>You use the first conditional with If clauses to talk about real possibilities in the future.</p><p>You use the second conditional to talk about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the First Conditional to say it's possible that you will do or not do something. In that condition, something else may, will or will not happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The parts of the sentence are divided into two clauses: the <span class=\"italic\">If</span> clause and the <span class=\"italic\">Condition</span> clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Second Conditional to talk about hypothetical situations. It's not certain that it's possible to fulfill the condition."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">If I had a million dollars, I would buy a car.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Do you have a million dollars?  No. <br/>Is it possible to suddenly get a million dollars? Not really.<br/>What would you do if you had a million dollars? Buy a car."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past verb + <span class=\"italic\">would</span></span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">First Conditional:<br/>1st Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">First Conditional:<br/>2nd Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If people show more respect for nature,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">everybody will be able to live peacefully with it.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's possible that people show more respect for nature. In this condition, everybody will be able to live peacefully. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Second Conditional:<br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> ... + Simple Past</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Second Conditional:<br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">would</span> + base verb</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Result</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If we ignored her commitment to the environment,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">her campaigning would be in vain.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is not certain that we ignore her commitment. What would happen if it did? Her campaigning would be in vain.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Questions within Sentences"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You ask for clarification when you want more details of what the other person is talking about."}, {"type": "text", "content": "We often ask for clarification when we are not clear on what the other person is referring to. We ask the other person to be more specific by giving more information. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use questions with sentences to ask for clarification. You ask a question including a sentence within the question, like <span class=\"italic\">Do you know if anything motivated Rachel Carson to become an activist?</span> <br/>Questions with sentences are called <span class=\"strong\">embedded questions.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">embedded questions</span>, like <span class=\"italic\">Can you tell me ... ?</span> or <span class=\"italic\">Do you know if / which / what ... ?</span> to ask for clarification.<br/>Look at the chart below for an explanation on how to make embedded questions."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Main Question</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Embedded Question</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Do you know ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"what / where / when / who / ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Do you remember ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"what / where / when / who / ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Can you tell me ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"what / where / when / who / ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Could you tell me ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"what / where / when / who / ... ?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do you remember the first time you felt inspired by Carson's actions?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can you tell us what happened afterwards?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sanctuary"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a place of refuge or safety"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Rachel Carson became an activist after she visited a bird sanctuary."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about the importance of speaking out for the protection of the environment."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to spray"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to apply a liquid or gas in the form of a shower of tiny drops or particles"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She found out that a local government agency sprayed an enormous amount of harmful substance in the air."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pesticide"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a substance used to destroy insects and other harmful organisms"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She found out that a local government agency sprayed an enormous amount of pesticide."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "compelled"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "forced or obliged to do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She felt compelled to investigate."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "evidence"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the available facts indicating a belief is valid; proof"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If she found evidence about what caused the animals to die, she would be able to prove that pesticides were harmful to the earth."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "controversial"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "likely to raise public disagreement"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She published a book on her findings, which became controversial."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fanatic"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "showing excessive enthusiasm in something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Environmentalists stressed the importance of her work, while chemical companies dubbed her a fanatic."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob03aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le17ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Begin with a sentence, for example: <span class=\"italic\">\u201cIf I won a million dollars, I would travel around the world.\u201d</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Your partner must use the end of the previous sentence to begin their own sentence. <span class=\"italic\">\u201cIf I traveled around the world , I would visit Japan.\u201d</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Continue back and forth with your partner for five rounds."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Start your chain using one of these prompts: <ul><li>If I won the lottery ...</li>  <li>If I were the leader of my country ...</li> <li>If I visited the U.S. next week ...</li></ul>"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I  talk about feelings and impressions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I  exchange opinions. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I  talk about hypothetical situations."}]}], "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can 