 "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn7le17ob03re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: John, do you remember the first time you felt inspired by Carson's actions?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">John Smits</span>: Certainly. With the publication of <span class=\"italic\">The Sea Around Us</span> in 1951, Carson was able to devote all of her time to writing. This quote summarizes her goal: if people show more respect for nature, everybody will be able to live peacefully with it.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn7le17ob03re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Do you know if anything motivated her to become an activist?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">John Smits</span>: It all began with a letter from a friend who owned a bird sanctuary. She found out that a local government agency sprayed an enormous amount of pesticide, killing many birds. She felt compelled to investigate. She believed that if she found evidence about what caused the animals to die, she would be able to prove that pesticides were harmful to the earth.", "id": 2, "time": "22000", "image": "engenn7le17ob03re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Can you tell us what happened afterwards?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">John Smits</span>: She published a book on her findings, which became controversial. Environmentalists stressed the importance of her work, while chemical companies dubbed her a fanatic. Nevertheless, a study later demonstrated that her facts were correct.", "id": 3, "time": "47200", "image": "engenn7le17ob03re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Do you think that Carson is still relevant today?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">John Smits</span>: Absolutely. Her work is compelling. If we ignored her commitment to the environment, her campaigning against the death of American wildlife would be in vain.", "id": 4, "time": "66000", "image": "engenn7le17ob03re2img05.jpg"}]}}]}]}], "type": "sena"}